Z||000000||86SE||03-17-2000||10:37 PM||||My aunts 87 sunbirds check engine light comes on and i want to run a diagnostic for her but I dont know where the diag. block is or what codes they are when they start blinking.<P>I was thinking, since its a '87, does it use the same computer as the '87 Fiero??  So could I use the same codes??<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||kupop87gt||03-18-2000||12:44 AM||||There must be a Hayne's manual for the car.<BR>I don't know about the computer... Are Fiero 4 and 6 cyl. engines operated by the same computer? What engine is in the Sunbird? I don't believe the J-bodies have ever used the 2.5||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-18-2000||12:49 AM||||The connector is under the dash just below the steering wheel. Some of them have a plastic cover over them. The codes are the same basically for all GM cars. There are a few codes for each type of engine that are specific. Like turbo engines have a couple of codes for the turbo components and such.<BR>But if you cannot find the code in your fiero book you can always go to the library and copy the codes from the service manual. Most libraries have these in the reference area. You can look and copy but you can't check them out. ||||reg||1
